From cd30398646f4fb48ed352a9d46a7b2d4747fc916 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:29:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 302/304] hir_conv: an alias parameter inferred at a value path
 head stays one inference variable

itertools 0.13.0 / 0.14.0 duplicates_impl.rs:216 (gitui 0.28.1), regression from 0297:
`pub type Duplicates<I> = private::DuplicatesBy<I, <I as Iterator>::Item, private::ById>;`
+ `Duplicates::new(iter, private::ById)` = "<null> BUG: src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp:8669:
Spare rules left after typecheck stabilised" with `<I as Iterator>::Item = <_/*2*/ as
Iterator>::Item`, `_/*2*/: Iterator` left over.

The omitted `I` is one `_` node shared by both of its uses in the alias expansion, and
typeck's add_ivars gives the node its ivar in place. 0297's fill_alias_type_defaults
called get_unique() on every node of the expansion (copy-on-write, needed to edit a path
shared with the alias's own type) and so split the `_` into two unrelated ivars; only the
first got `= I` from the argument. Infer nodes are never copied there now.

Assisted-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp b/src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp
index 57cd300b..fcd9e2f0 100644
--- a/src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_conv/expand_type.cpp
@@ -79,6 +79,12 @@ namespace {
             V(const Span& sp, const ::HIR::Crate& crate): sp(sp), crate(crate) {}
             void visit_type(::HIR::TypeRef& ty) override
             {
+                // An omitted parameter is one `_` node shared by every use of that parameter in the expansion
+                // (`type Duplicates<I> = DuplicatesBy<I, <I as Iterator>::Item, ById>` + `Duplicates::new(iter, ById)`):
+                // typeck gives the node its ivar in place, so a copy here would be a second, unrelated ivar
+                // (itertools 0.14.0 duplicates_impl.rs:216: `Spare rules left after typecheck stabilised`).
+                if( ty.data().is_Infer() )
+                    return ;
                 // The expansion shares nodes with the alias's own type (TypeRef copies are shallow)
                 ty.get_unique();
                 ::HIR::Visitor::visit_type(ty);
